{%- comment -%}
  The bag's checkout control, in whichever form the merchant's checkout setting
  calls for.

  Three destinations:

  - Shopify checkout — a submit button named `checkout`, which is what Shopify's
    cart form expects.
  - The merchant's own order form — a real anchor, not a button wired up with
    script. Middle-click, open-in-new-tab and "copy link" all work, and it needs
    no JavaScript to function. Common wherever cash on delivery is collected by
    an app rather than by Shopify.
  - Nowhere — a demo store. Stays a button so the layout is unchanged, and
    jogger.js intercepts it.

  Accepts:
  - class {String} classes for the control
  - style {String} inline style, optional
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign mode = settings.checkout_mode | default: 'shopify'
  assign form_url = settings.checkout_url

  comment
    A custom destination with no address set would strand the shopper on a dead
    control, so it falls back to Shopify's own checkout until one is entered.
  endcomment
  assign use_form = false
  if mode == 'custom' and form_url != blank
    assign use_form = true
  endif
-%}

{%- if use_form -%}
  <a href="{{ form_url }}" class="{{ class }}" {% if style %}style="{{ style }}"{% endif %}>
    {{ 'sections.cart.checkout' | t }}
    <span class="ar">&rarr;</span>
  </a>
{%- else -%}
  <button type="submit" name="checkout" class="{{ class }}" {% if style %}style="{{ style }}"{% endif %}>
    {{ 'sections.cart.checkout' | t }}
    <span class="ar">&rarr;</span>
  </button>
{%- endif -%}
